{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle","id":1545674,"title":"[MtAw Dark Eras] Integration of Tremere \u2013 700-1100 AD [Tome of Pentacle]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-10T21:12:43-08:00","id":1545674,"title":"[MtAw Dark Eras] Integration of Tremere \u2013 700-1100 AD [Tome of Pentacle]","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Topic on the whole scoops on Tremere joining Diamond 5 Orders then. <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> is sparse on info of those events. Even <b>Nameless and Accursed</b> only sum-up it simply. And I still have questions on subject\u2026</span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>HOW Tremere join instantly all Europes Consillia of Diamond?</b> Was there some Convocation to accept them, like there was in Alexandria in 265 AD that <b><i>created</i></b> Diamond Alliance in first place?</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>I suspect what\u2019s 1E called</b> <i>\u2018and Tremere were knock on the doot of Eastern Europe lone tower to joined Diamond\u2019 </i>is Tremere taking <b><i>Fortress of Chur</i></b>, Time Before ruin, as Tremere Order personal headquarters?</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>\u2018Official\u2019 Vikings Age start from 792 AD </b>with the raid on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lindisfarne\" target=\"_blank\">Lindisfarne Abbey</a><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#71777d\">.</span></span> I think about story mixing joining of Tremere and \u2018start\u2019 ( maybe even \u2018secret start\u2019 ) of Vikings raids era. But I\u2019m still not sure how to do it. There would also need to be some acclamation of Tremere Order. Maybe that Tremere show up locally in England and forseen \u2018great wyrm of light\u2019, like from <b>13<sup>th</sup> Warrior</b> it was? <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83e\udd14</span> ( But weird would be that Tremere forseen it and other Acanthoi from other Orders would NOT seen it\u2026 ) Just idea.</span></li> </ol><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8p43qPuIM7E\" data-code=\"8p43qPuIM7E\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/8p43qPuIM7E/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-11-2024, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T01:43:36-08:00","id":1545679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle#post1545674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HOW Tremere join instantly all Europes Consillia of Diamond? Was there some Convocation to accept them, like there was in Alexandria in 265 AD that created Diamond Alliance in first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a reasonable inference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>I suspect what\u2019s 1E called</b> <i>\u2018and Tremere were knock on the doot of Eastern Europe lone tower to joined Diamond\u2019 </i>is Tremere taking <b><i>Fortress of Chur</i></b>, Time Before ruin, as Tremere Order personal headquarters?</span> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but if you're going to quote something, could you actually quote it? Or at least say where the quote is from?<br /> <br /> Like, that sounds like two sentences from p.78 of <i>Left-Hand Path:</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tremere Liches came out of Eastern Europe while it was still pagan. In the 8th century, one or two demanded hospitality at wizard's towers. </div> </div> </div>Which really doesn't sound like Chur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T00:40:38-08:00","id":1545732,"title":"","content":"If we take 2E context of Convocations and Consilii politics - and filter this quote from <b>Left-Hand Path</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tremere Liches came out of Eastern Europe while it was still pagan. In the 8th century, one or two demanded hospitality at wizard's towers. </div> </div> </div>We may got that <b><i>Tremere asked local Convocations to join <b>Diamo</b>nd</i></b>. As I cannot fantom Grand Convocation like in Alexandria in 265 CE - I assume Tremere went from Medium (? ) Convocation to Convocation in each Europe's country to join and generally was accepted, based on precedent from Eastern European one. <br /> <br /> I easily can see it could take about 20-40 years, maybe even more, with each Ordinary Convocation taking place about each 5 years for those kingdoms areas. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T01:33:40-08:00","id":1545734,"title":"","content":"I'd keep in mind that per the Silver Ladder Order book, Convocations at all levels are supposed to happen regularly. It's never been the case that the biggest ones stayed on schedule, a problem that became worse as the scope of the Orders increased, but it at least might theoretically be a basis for them to gather for something as big as debating a petition to join the Diamond.<br /> <br /> In any case, I think the population of the time might have been low and centralised enough to make such a coordinated approach by the Tremere feasible. I still think the line about towers is just referring to approaching cabals in their sanctums, and even then not strictly literal.<br /> <br /> I picture a scenario of many Tremere cabals approaching Diamond ones with friendly overtures and gifts and credentials and asking to put a good word in. Then those cabals take their experience back to caucus and convocation, a reputation builds up, and when it's apparent the Tremere want in they call a big meeting to debate and ultimately ratify that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T01:55:23-08:00","id":1548179,"title":"","content":"You know, re-reading the Tome of Pentacle and Nameless and Accursed, I can't help but think that Awakening Tremere somehow inherited the plot armor of their namesakes from Masquerade. I mean:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the Diamond discovered the Tremere were devouring the Reaper Legacies they relentlessly hunted and using those Left-Handed Arts for themselves, it banished them from its ranks. On their way out, the Tremere stole or destroyed evidence of their membership and all detailed information about themselves, locking away histories and scrubbing records (and memories). Over time, remaining knowledge of the Order\u2019s fate became myth, which became superstition, which became vague rumors of a wicked Legacy of Reaper liches. Discovering the truth would be a controversial Mystery for the modern Pentacle. </div> </div> </div>I mean, this is so ridiculously overpowered, I don't even have words for it. Like, for that to happen, they would have to break into <b>each</b> Mouseion of Keepers of the Word, and scrub memory of <b>each</b> Adept or Master in whole Diamond - I can't imagine any lesser feat to remove whole <b>Order</b> from history. Does anyone has any other explanation beyond &quot;Tremere are just <i>better</i> than whole Diamond combined&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-04T05:33:24-08:00","id":1548183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548179#post1548179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, this is so ridiculously overpowered, I don't even have words for it. Like, for that to happen, they would have to break into <b>each</b> Mouseion of Keepers of the Word, and scrub memory of <b>each</b> Adept or Master in whole Diamond - I can't imagine any lesser feat to remove whole <b>Order</b> from history. Does anyone has any other explanation beyond &quot;Tremere are just <i>better</i> than whole Diamond combined&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Human mortality and the fact that the Orders do not generally have knowledge of each other's secrets nor share that information (nor other information) broadly, particularly not before the advent of modern communications technology when news of covert and/or self-hiding action like the removal of knowledge by a small and far-scattered former Order with no centralized Caucus leadership has few avenues of travel to reach the grapevine by the nature of the event.<br /> <br /> The Tremere joined the Diamond on their own terms over 1300 years ago and were expelled 400 years later, before and during which time they were known primarily as an Order of monster hunters with a habit of antagonizing the Keepers. The Apocalypse Mysteriorum, which would be the point where the Keepers' knowledge base would logically start being integrated with the Pancryptiates' techniques to give rise to the Mysterium's Egregore, did not happen for another 150 years. It's a point of lore that by modern day many mages learn rote mudras without being taught the deeper meanings of their symbolism, and Mage being a game about seeking out hidden knowledge does not negate (and rather relies upon) the fact that the Chronicles of Darkness are a setting where true and full information about supernatural topics is obscured and buried behind layers of misinformation, disinformation, and rumor.<br /> <br /> The Scions of the Seventh Watchtower were led by the same sorts of beings who went on to become its sole membership after they were exposed as Reapers. They could live forever on a diet of souls, innately have a subtler Nimbus and aura than other mages, and institutionally get Occultation along with Subterfuge as a Rote Skill. The part of their lore that got passed down \u2014 that they were soul-eating liches \u2014 is easy to propagate compared to the more detailed knowledge that would've been known about their practices and beliefs and the elements of their history that were dangerous to the ones in a position to share them \u2014 that they were part of the Diamond and considered the subject-matter experts on the soul and how unAwakened monsters affect it \u2014 which the Diamond itself had reason to keep quiet on for the same reason it doesn't advertise how easy it is to Befoul a spell. &quot;Steal a few treatises and memories and wait six to ten longish mortal lifetimes for the heat to die down&quot; does not beggar credibility as a feat for an organization whose upper echelons have &quot;reach the equivalent of the top third of the Gnosis ladder and wipe out and symbolically subjugate a Legacy that messes with souls&quot; as a prerequisite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Correcting typos and finishing a sentence. 02-05-2025, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T05:05:09-08:00","id":1548217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548183#post1548183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Apocalypse Mysteriorum, which would be the point where the Keepers' knowledge base would logically start being integrated with the Pancryptiates' techniques to give rise to the Mysterium's Egregore, did not happen for another 150 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even before rise of Egregore, Keepers had multiple ways to preserve their knowledge base. They had Scriptors to store their knowledge. In case Scriptors would be killed, they had Savants. In case both were killed, there are multitudes of ways to store that information basically forever - with a little help of Arcana. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548183#post1548183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">fact that the Orders do not generally have knowledge of each other's secrets nor share that information (nor other information) broadly, particularly not before the advent of modern communications technology</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't had to share it with <i>other </i>Orders; sharing it sufficiently wide in their own Order would be enough. Even if other Diamond Orders would not do it, Keepers certainly would. They had <i>Shared Knowledge</i> as their main symbolism point; I really doubt that such important and basic information as <i>existence and beliefs of a whole Diamond Order</i> would not be spread far and wide. Even in Middle Ages, Diamond Orders already were a global phenomenon; I don't really see why, for example, Chinese proto-Athenea wouldn't hold that information. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548183#post1548183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part of their lore that got passed down \u2014 that they were soul-eating liches \u2014 is easy to propagate compared to the more detailed knowledge that would've been known about their practices and beliefs and the elements of their history that were dangerous to the ones in a position to share them \u2014 that they were part of the Diamond and considered the subject-matter experts on the soul and how unAwakened monsters affect it \u2014 which the Diamond itself had reason to keep quiet on for the same reason it doesn't advertise how easy it is to Befoul a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That more detailed knowledge is still very easily summed up, as the book Nameless and Accursed witnesses by itself. Besides, it's very hard to compare Befouling spells - something <i>every</i> mage can do, with a bit of know-how and practice, and very dangerous consequences - and a bit of trivia about long-dead Order. I don't really see basis for such comparison to be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T06:07:28-08:00","id":1548218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548217#post1548217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even before rise of Egregore, Keepers had multiple ways to preserve their knowledge base. They had Scriptors to store their knowledge. In case Scriptors would be killed, they had Savants. In case both were killed, there are multitudes of ways to store that information basically forever - with a little help of Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody needs to be killed. Records going missing and memories being erased just requires infiltration, and the Tremere already had a reputation for messing with the recordkeeping Order before they got exposed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They didn't had to share it with <i>other </i>Orders; sharing it sufficiently wide in their own Order would be enough. Even if other Diamond Orders would not do it, Keepers certainly would. They had <i>Shared Knowledge</i> as their main symbolism point; I really doubt that such important and basic information as <i>existence and beliefs of a whole Diamond Order</i> would not be spread far and wide. Even in Middle Ages, Diamond Orders already were a global phenomenon; I don't really see why, for example, Chinese proto-Athenea wouldn't hold that information. </div> </div> </div>Shared Knowledge <i>as a bulwark against it dying out</i> was their main point of symbolism, and that was manifested in a focus on <i>teaching</i>. The Keepers weren't the nightly news even if having a global distribution and magical lines of communication did anything to guarantee copies of information about a group that was trying to swiss-cheese other people's knowledge of who was a soul-eating Reaper and what exactly they were capable of (to say nothing of the obvious incentives against spreading information globally using magic in a setting where magical memetic hazards are a known phenomenon).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That more detailed knowledge is still very easily summed up, as the book Nameless and Accursed witnesses by itself. Besides, it's very hard to compare Befouling spells - something <i>every</i> mage can do, with a bit of know-how and practice, and very dangerous consequences - and a bit of trivia about long-dead Order. I don't really see basis for such comparison to be made. </div> </div> </div>The Tremere are the primary reason researching the soul is a bit of a taboo in modern times and &quot;the Tremere derive substantial benefits from stealing souls&quot; is the sort of thing you do not want apprentices eager for shortcuts to power knowing about.<br /> <br /> The Guardians have had multiple disquieting doctrines described within their ranks, including some of the Factions listed in Tome of the Pentacle. If it can be believed that the spycraft Order can keep the modern Mysterium from spreading the word that their secret tenets include undermining all Awakened leadership in the name of a messianic secret hierarchy (much less that a subset of their membership thinks they're living in the post-Rapture and need to kill everyone to get to the true world), it can be believed that the secret soul-eating hardcore soul-research crew who can all get Mind as a Ruling Arcanum could infiltrate magical libraries for long enough to delete names from dossiers and memory-hole details about their beliefs and practices long enough to outlast their human lifespan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T06:39:30-08:00","id":1548219,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548218#post1548218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody needs to be killed. Records going missing and memories being erased just requires infiltration, and the Tremere already had a reputation for messing with the recordkeeping Order before they got exposed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infiltration so total and complete why managed to do this against whole Order without single point of failure? Ridiculously overpowered, IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548218#post1548218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shared Knowledge <i>as a bulwark against it dying out</i> was their main point of symbolism, and that was manifested in a focus on <i>teaching</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Focus on teaching does not forbid <i>protecting</i> knowledge. In fact, it is as important as teaching, and it shows in Keepers of the Word description:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The oldest and most organized Diamond Order, the Keepers of the Word \u2014 also known as Sacristans \u2014 collect and <b>stand guard</b> over the collective knowledge of humanity </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Order sees itself as tending that flame \u2014 saving ideas from the originating mind on behalf of future generations, husbanding Logos\u2019 growth over the centuries.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Kind of hard to do so if knowledge is destroyed by someone hubristic enough to do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548218#post1548218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere are the primary reason researching the soul is a bit of a taboo in modern times and &quot;the Tremere derive substantial benefits from stealing souls&quot; is the sort of thing you do not want apprentices eager for shortcuts to power knowing about.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this knowledge isn't even well-hidden? It is known that Tremere were a Legacy of Reaper-Liches; it's simple jump of thought from there to &quot;well, they had some kind of power from it, didn't they?&quot;. Amongst Diamond Belt mages, it is well-known fact that one can use soul for powering up spells. And so on. If information about Tremere was hidden for that reason, it would be logical to hide the fact they were Reaper-Liches, not the fact that there was a Diamond order of monster hunter which went rogue and was banished.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548218#post1548218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guardians have had multiple disquieting doctrines described within their ranks, including some of the Factions listed in Tome of the Pentacle. If it can be believed that the spycraft Order can keep the modern Mysterium from spreading the word that their secret tenets include undermining all Awakened leadership in the name of a messianic secret hierarchy (much less that a subset of their membership thinks they're living in the post-Rapture and need to kill everyone to get to the true world), it can be believed that the secret soul-eating hardcore soul-research crew who can all get Mind as a Ruling Arcanum could infiltrate magical libraries for long enough to delete names from dossiers and memory-hole details about their beliefs and practices long enough to outlast their human lifespan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be believed precisely because Guardians are a <i>spycraft</i> Order, building their whole praxis around lies, infiltration and misdirection, <i>and</i> because if modern Mysterium would know the truth, it would probably hide it anyways out of fear of breaking Pentacle and losing one of their greatest allies in a battle against Seers. Tremere aren't spycraft Order; having Subterfuge as a Rote Skill doesn't make them one. As for the last argument - yeah, if you take it as a fact that Tremere are just <i><b>better </b></i>than other Diamond mages - they have higher Gnosis analogue on average, they have Mind as Ruling Arcanum, and all of this outweighs the magical power of rest of Diamond - then this works out. But I was looking for some other explanation other than that one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T09:27:23-08:00","id":1548226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548219#post1548219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infiltration so total and complete why managed to do this against whole Order without single point of failure? Ridiculously overpowered, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nine hundred years of entropy can, in fact, account for a concerted effort to conceal information about the secrets of a former ally before the full details of their betrayal incentivized the deeper safeguarding of that information when both parties are hidden mystery cults in the eleventh century. The Orders sharing doctrine does not make them monoliths in every location, much less guarantee all information was in all locations or provide an ironclad wall against its removal or alteration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Focus on teaching does not forbid <i>protecting</i> knowledge. In fact, it is as important as teaching, and it shows in Keepers of the Word description:<br /> <br /> Kind of hard to do so if knowledge is destroyed by someone hubristic enough to do that. </div> </div> </div>The Keepers keeping and protecting knowledge does not guarantee that knowledge is not lost over the course of 900 years. Accidents happen and the Tremere are known in the modern day as a largely isolated Legacy of soul-eaters rather than an organized collection of Houses with an anti-Watchtower ideology and origins in an extended Captivity by other monsters, with the ability to copy Nimbuses and enter suspended animation for decades, and the capacity to physically handle souls, the chance of turning into ghoulish ex-mage monsters in the wrong circumstances. Their Houses don't provide sympathetic connections between their members like Legacies do and their Nameless Order's culture is conspiratorial and transactional at best. Boogeymen who don't show up too often get their stories warped and seldom get their files updated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But this knowledge isn't even well-hidden? It is known that Tremere were a Legacy of Reaper-Liches; it's simple jump of thought from there to &quot;well, they had some kind of power from it, didn't they?&quot;. Amongst Diamond Belt mages, it is well-known fact that one can use soul for powering up spells. And so on. If information about Tremere was hidden for that reason, it would be logical to hide the fact they were Reaper-Liches, not the fact that there was a Diamond order of monster hunter which went rogue and was banished. </div> </div> </div>The Tremere are the primary reason the Diamond uses &quot;X of the Dragon&quot; symbolism and gain their greatest benefits from one of them distinguishing themselves by eating another Reaper Legacy. They can functionally disguise themselves as a dead body for years and the ones who manage to make it in the group have it impressed upon them that their membership is secret even if the taboo against tampering with souls wasn't already a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It can be believed precisely because Guardians are a <i>spycraft</i> Order, building their whole praxis around lies, infiltration and misdirection, <i>and</i> because if modern Mysterium would know the truth, it would probably hide it anyways out of fear of breaking Pentacle and losing one of their greatest allies in a battle against Seers. Tremere aren't spycraft Order; having Subterfuge as a Rote Skill doesn't make them one. As for the last argument - yeah, if you take it as a fact that Tremere are just <i><b>better </b></i>than other Diamond mages - they have higher Gnosis analogue on average, they have Mind as Ruling Arcanum, and all of this outweighs the magical power of rest of Diamond - then this works out. </div> </div> </div>The Tremere get an extra Subtle Ruling Arcanum for every other dot of Hollow, institutionally provide the benefits of the main bulwark against sympathetic magic before they provide Rote Skills, are incentivized to be good at lying and disguise and manipulation by virtue of two of their Rote Skills, and were considered the subject-matter experts in the depredations of non-Supernal beings on the human soul, and before their expulsion the lower ranks of their Order were mechanically indistinguishable from other Diamond mages who might conceivably requisition documents on the Tremere and either never return them or alter them.<br /> <br /> The Tremere don't have to have power outweighing that of the entire rest of the Diamond, they need have been good enough in the past to make a focused push to destroy or seal away information about themselves well enough that people forget the details. The Keepers were one Order among six that merged with another Order and deliberately purged a bunch of information from their archives during that merger, and organizations are made of people who are fallible and lack perfect information at all times. We know the Tremere were banished from the Diamond; we do not know the full circumstances of how that banishment was carried out, nor the details of how the Tremere scratched the record on their way out, but the Chronicles of Darkness are not a setting that is a stranger to heists, sabotage, or sudden magical disasters that remove concrete knowledge from the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T19:42:54-08:00","id":1548243,"title":"","content":"I think it can be attributed to some combination of &quot;needing to rebuild some things from scratch is not trivial&quot;, &quot;there are ways to make books that actually did continue to exist become lost for hundreds of years, a thing that has happened in reality (and in character provides plot hooks for rediscovery of lost lore&quot; and &quot;how many mages do you think existed in Europe in the 11th century?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548217#post1548217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That more detailed knowledge is still very easily summed up, as the book Nameless and Accursed witnesses by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it to be a basic conceit of roleplaying games that the kinds of barebones summaries that function for the purposes of conveying what is necessary to roleplay are not particularly useful in character.<br /> <br /> It's like getting a three line summary of how a black hole works, something far below the standards necessary to actually participate in real academic study of them. Cross that over with the idea that mages have often not had the infrastructure to preserve and promote a three line summary, and have often not actually wanted to.<br /> <br /> Still, there's a more key question that underlies all of this; is one actually looking for explanations that can provide consistency and integrity with a setting (having made maybe a few reasonable allowances for artistic licence and suspension of disbelief), or is the main priority to outsmart the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T20:11:00-08:00","id":1548244,"title":"","content":"There are a few other things worth considering.<br /> <br /> One is that it's probably kind of difficult writing fictional equivalents to a lot of grand historical events. Logically, the in-character process of that would have had a lot of things that were touch and go in the moment which, by virtue of the fact that they end up working, makes them superficially look like unstoppable juggernauts. In real life, people often don't know the deeper intricacies of those things, but they can maintain credibility by virtue of the fact that they actually happened.<br /> <br /> As far as the extent of magical defences and countermeasures go, I feel as though in these kinds of discussions people often assume mages have endless time and means to apply as many possible back ups and contingencies as possible so as to make any kind of assault on them basically impossible. And they forget things like the limits of spell control and the high costs of relinquishment and even just the idea that an accumulation of mages will want to be focused on things other than doing that. That's the kind of thing that really needs to cultivate a setting picture of &quot;mages are actually very sparing and strategic about where they apply things like their long term spells&quot;, with just a dash of &quot;the best defence is that nobody actually wants to attack you 99% of the time&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, well... for better or for worse, suppressing or ending spells is something that can be done with one dot of Prime and one other Arcanum. And the necessary Potency is based on a fixed rate for the mage who originally cast it, rather than something they might put a lot of extra time and effort into reinforcing. There are sharp limits to the extent to which mages can expect their spells to protect things from other mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T22:15:24-08:00","id":1548284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548244#post1548244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the extent of magical defences and countermeasures go, I feel as though in these kinds of discussions people often assume mages have endless time and means to apply as many possible back ups and contingencies as possible so as to make any kind of assault on them basically impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do assume that mages enchant their Sanctums with the best protective magic they have at the very least, yes. And they also tend to stack it up as generations go, passing it from one cabal generation to another one. I do think there are canonical examples of that going, but even if not - this makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548244#post1548244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they forget things like the limits of spell control and the high costs of relinquishment and even just the idea that an accumulation of mages will want to be focused on things other than doing that. That's the kind of thing that really needs to cultivate a setting picture of &quot;mages are actually very sparing and strategic about where they apply things like their long term spells&quot;, with just a dash of &quot;the best defence is that nobody actually wants to attack you 99% of the time&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't forget this, but for me it's simple - the benefit of having permanent enchantments on yourself and Sanctums far, far outweighs any inconveniences you have to go through to achieve that. So you use Sacrificial Relinquishment (or worse analogues, if you have the stomach to do it), or you relinquish unsafely with as little Reach as practical and periodically clean up the spells which start to show damage to recast them, or you suck it up and burn some EXP. I can easily see Awakened gathering lots of Sleepwalkers to hold up their defenses. In my games, you can actually buy Sanctum Sanctorum and bind spell to extra slot it gives, and/or use Node to bind spell to geomancy supporting it. <br /> <br /> Where there is will, there is a way. Willworkers do not lack will, by definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548244#post1548244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, well... for better or for worse, suppressing or ending spells is something that can be done with one dot of Prime and one other Arcanum. And the necessary Potency is based on a fixed rate for the mage who originally cast it, rather than something they might put a lot of extra time and effort into reinforcing. There are sharp limits to the extent to which mages can expect their spells to protect things from other mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>This merits only addition of Wards and Signs or analogous spell to protect other spells from enchantment. Possibly as a combined spell, maybe as a spell on &quot;top&quot; of other defences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T10:31:40-08:00","id":1548292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548284#post1548284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do assume that mages enchant their Sanctums with the best protective magic they have at the very least, yes. And they also tend to stack it up as generations go, passing it from one cabal generation to another one. I do think there are canonical examples of that going, but even if not - this makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183342-what-am-i-missing-about-the-sanctum-merit\">So we're back to this again, huh.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't forget this, but for me it's simple - the benefit of having permanent enchantments on yourself and Sanctums far, far outweighs any inconveniences you have to go through to achieve that. So you use Sacrificial Relinquishment (or worse analogues, if you have the stomach to do it), or you relinquish unsafely with as little Reach as practical and periodically clean up the spells which start to show damage to recast them, or you suck it up and burn some EXP. I can easily see Awakened gathering lots of Sleepwalkers to hold up their defenses. In my games, you can actually buy Sanctum Sanctorum and bind spell to extra slot it gives, and/or use Node to bind spell to geomancy supporting it. </div> </div> </div>You are a Keeper Caucus. The year is 1099. There are less than a third of a billion people in the entire world. The movable-type printing press is centuries away from being invented, with paper being not much closer in history. In the distant future, the number of mages in the world will be determined to have not gone up proportionately to the Sleeper population. Every non-Imperial spell that runs out or is dispelled needs to be re-cast by a mage, physical libraries take up physical space and/or magical resources to maintain, to say nothing of any contributing Sleepwalkers still being people with lives and needs, and the world is such that archmasters don't relinquish the spells generating their subsouls specifically because maintaining spell control is a nontrivial benefit.<br /> <br /> Somehow, the tiny Order of monster-hunters who keep messing with you has been revealed to be stealing the secrets of the Reaper Legacies they have been hunting and have been declared Left-Handed. Serves them right, to be sure, but this news is coming through the grapevine on what accelerated timescales are likely to occur through sympathetic magic from mages that think it's worth sharing immediately, and more slowly though other channels.<br /> <br /> If they got caught they mustn't have been making plans for the eventuality of being found out, right? Surely the folks who believe Magic Must be Tamed wouldn't have taken notes on your security when they were buzzing your records rooms as a prank. You were definitely keeping copies of the book that their own apprentices weren't allowed to read in a maximum security vault before they might have an incentive to steal their membership rosters, right? None of the ones that you interviewed however many decades ago were being untruthful? And you're definitely sure that your memory is accurate and all your neighboring Mouseions were equally certain in the security they've placed this specific information under across the centuries that these liches have been another branch of your shared organization that has more prominent concerns than sabotage from within. Nothing could go wrong.<br /> <br /> The year is 1099 and you are a magical librarian and your master's wards are perfect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where there is will, there is a way. Willworkers do not lack will, by definition. </div> </div> </div>And the most common means of relinquishing spells entails giving up a bit of your will that you need to dedicate further time to recovering that you could instead spend on actual advancement or, god forbid, regular day-to-day living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This merits only addition of Wards and Signs or analogous spell to protect other spells from enchantment. Possibly as a combined spell, maybe as a spell on &quot;top&quot; of other defences. </div> </div> </div>So in this world where the Keepers have infinite prep time and knowledge of every spell within their Arcana as a rote or praxis with which to permanently ward off any threat to their knowledge base that couldn't overcome them without OP hax, which are preserved across nearly a millennium despite the likely eventual death of every Keeper of the Word who could remember them past the Apocalypse, what alternative explanation do you have for how the Tremere went from being part of the Diamond for a goodly chunk of the Early Middle Ages to being known as a bogeyman Legacy of soul-stealing liches with no attached ideology or organization in modern nights?<br /> <br /> Surely another Alexandrian fire isn't the culprit after the first one wiped out a bunch of knowledge, but the Diamond demonstrably doesn't know (or at least doesn't have as common knowledge) that the Tremere are still around today as a conspiracy of fully pseudo-vampiric Houses, so did the Seventh Dragon just stamp its conceptual feet all over the record pages and make everybody forget?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T11:09:20-08:00","id":1548297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548179#post1548179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, re-reading the Tome of Pentacle and Nameless and Accursed, I can't help but think that Awakening Tremere somehow inherited the plot armor of their namesakes from Masquerade. I mean:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, this is so ridiculously overpowered, I don't even have words for it. Like, for that to happen, they would have to break into <b>each</b> Mouseion of Keepers of the Word, and scrub memory of <b>each</b> Adept or Master in whole Diamond - I can't imagine any lesser feat to remove whole <b>Order</b> from history. Does anyone has any other explanation beyond &quot;Tremere are just <i>better</i> than whole Diamond combined&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're gonna cite TotP on what the Tremere did on the way out, you might also want to cite what the timeline says on the subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tome of the Pentacle, Chapter 1, pg 30, The Diamond Yuga: The Draconic Age</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1099 CE: At the Convocation of Antioch, Lady Catarine Beldam, called the Wildcat, exposes the Tremere as Reapers. The Legacy\u2019s mages are declared nefandi and expelled. <u><b>What influence of their membership the Diamond doesn\u2019t erase</b></u>, the Tremere steal or destroy themselves on their way out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere aren't masterminding some heist of the Diamond's record of their time with them and performing a sweeping power play. THey're sweeping up the crumbs left by the Diamond doing that to themselves, which is a pretty effective cover for any remaining patsies and subversives to operate under and do that very thing with.<br /> <br /> It also pays to remember that this self-purgation likely has a second phase later with the Mysterium Reformation bringing in a new wave of self-censorship as the Pancryptiate influence is applied to Keeper Mouseions-Mysterium Censors and Curators are not above destroying records and artifacts they feel are problematic, and that first purge answers that.<br /> <br /> So not so much OP as being an effective janitor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T13:49:03-08:00","id":1548305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548284#post1548284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think there are canonical examples of that going, but even if not - this makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense, up until you encounter a piece of setting writing that is incompatible with your assumptions, at which point the setting is wrong and your assumptions are correct?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't forget this, but for me it's simple - the benefit of having permanent enchantments on yourself and Sanctums far, far outweighs any inconveniences you have to go through to achieve that. So you use Sacrificial Relinquishment (or worse analogues, if you have the stomach to do it), or you relinquish unsafely with as little Reach as practical and periodically clean up the spells which start to show damage to recast them, or you suck it up and burn some EXP.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit contrary to design intentions, but even if your own priorities would find the spells preferable, a mage only has so many Willpower points to give up (or other things to sacrifice). And constantly returning to spells is a bit time inefficient.<br /> <br /> As far as Sleepwalkers go, that helps, but creates a bit of a liability in somebody that might be vulnerable to being targeted to disrupt the spell.<br /> <br /> House rules are probably not something that setting writers could account for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where there is will, there is a way. Willworkers do not lack will, by definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why not apply this to the will of the Tremere to go underground, particularly since that might be a much more proactive intention than preventing the Tremere from obscuring the manner in which they went underground?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T19:33:36-08:00","id":1548387,"title":"","content":"See, and here I thought that all of that mess was because of the aponoia and other imperial shenanigans of the one and only Archliche Tremere reaching Archmastery and retconning and erasing reality bits (accidentally and on purpose) in the process of Imperium and the gathering of Quintessence he needed to shove his OWoD crossover into reality kicking and screaming, using Entities to forge his liches out of the now-mostly-dead non-tremere liches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T19:49:28-08:00","id":1548388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548387#post1548387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, and here I thought that all of that mess was because of the aponoia and other imperial shenanigans of the one and only Archliche Tremere reaching Archmastery and retconning and erasing reality bits (accidentally and on purpose) in the process of Imperium and the gathering of Quintessence he needed to shove his OWoD crossover into reality kicking and screaming, using Entities to forge his liches out of the now-mostly-dead non-tremere liches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny what reading the text actually does!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T19:49:34-08:00","id":1548389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545674-mtaw-dark-eras-integration-of-tremere-\u2013-700-1100-ad-tome-of-pentacle?p=1548387#post1548387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, and here I thought that all of that mess was because of the aponoia and other imperial shenanigans of the one and only Archliche Tremere reaching Archmastery and retconning and erasing reality bits (accidentally and on purpose) in the process of Imperium and the gathering of Quintessence he needed to shove his OWoD crossover into reality kicking and screaming, using Entities to forge his liches out of the now-mostly-dead non-tremere liches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmaster and reality editing stuff is neat, but it's a problem if all major historical processes in the setting are shifted in their direction. Most stuff of relevance to the development of the history of the Chronicles of Darkness world takes place at the resolution of the characters you will most typically play.<br /> <br /> Even the actual book that gave us a peek under the hood of how archmstery worked, and its implications for the larger cosmos, was built around a core of archmasters being mostly background characters in the ongoing events of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T22:24:36-08:00","id":1548422,"title":"","content":"Almost reminds of the aliens of Dark City who would rewrite reality and were the secret masters of the world<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T07:03:20-08:00","id":1548431,"title":"","content":"The Keepers of the Word were the least friendly Orderbto the Tremere, and they were the Order who allowed anyone to use their archives as long as they paid for it.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium absolutely restricts knowledge to individuals they think are worthy of it and responsible enough for it, are enthusiatic about ring-fencing banned topics outside of the sources they control, and purged the Keepers' archives they inherited so thoroughly the period is called &quot;the bonfire&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Diamond didn't accidentally forgrt the Tremere. They did it very deliberately.<br /> <br /> It's their go-to response for magical traditions they disapprove of. See also; Scelesti practices, the more-entangled-than-admitted Seer history and practices. The more entangled-than-admitted Nameless history and practices, etcetera.<br /> <br /> Fake edit to add - I mean, Paternoster started as an Adamantine Arrow heresy, the Arrow are the Order who collect intelligence on external enemies, and they don't have any special insights. They'd much rather pretend Veritas was a Seer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T10:29:00-08:00","id":1548439,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think one might look at the fact that it took until the middle of the 20th century for the Pentacle to even have a consolidated idea of what the Rapt were and conclude that the Awakened are often not great at forming conclusions based on collaborative information sharing.<br /> <br /> That one also, probably not coincidentally, being a matter of something abhorrent arising out of a likely source of shame for any mages that ever become personally involved with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}